(function(E){ const x = E["exam-05"] = E["exam-05"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x05-r2"] = {"id":"x05-r2","patterns":["RA-nature","GT2-business","PARA-research","PARA-cause"],"title":{"en":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","tr":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","fa":"Reading ۲: متن ۲ (Passage 2) / بخش ۲ (Section 2)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which section contains a piece of information, to match statements to the researcher who made them, and to complete a summary with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, ifadeleri onları söyleyen araştırmacıyla eşleştirmeyi ve bir özeti metinden tek bir kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی یک اطلاعات در کدام بخش است، جمله‌ها را به پژوهشگری که گفته وصل کنی و یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete sentences and notes with one word from two work-related texts, keeping to the word limit and the exact form of the word.","tr":"Bu derste işle ilgili iki metinden tek bir kelimeyle cümleleri ve notları tamamlamayı, kelime sınırına ve kelimenin tam biçimine uymayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه از دو متن کاری کامل کنی و سقف کلمه و شکل دقیق کلمه را رعایت کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 2: a report with three researchers","tr":"Reading Passage 2: üç araştırmacılı bir rapor","fa":"Reading Passage 2: گزارشی با سه پژوهشگر"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which section contains a piece of information, to match statements to the researcher who made them, and to complete a summary with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, ifadeleri onları söyleyen araştırmacıyla eşleştirmeyi ve bir özeti metinden tek bir kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی یک اطلاعات در کدام بخش است، جمله‌ها را به پژوهشگری که گفته وصل کنی و یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-G"},{"label":{"en":"Researchers","tr":"Araştırmacı","fa":"پژوهشگر"},"value":"3"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: the wild apple","tr":"Bu sınav: yabani elma","fa":"این آزمون: سیب وحشی"},"intro":{"en":"Passage 2 is often a report on a scientific problem, divided into lettered sections, with several named experts. Nature and the environment are the most common subjects. Learn the research verbs on the card: they tell you whose view you are reading.","tr":"Passage 2 çoğu zaman bilimsel bir sorun üzerine, harfli bölümlere ayrılmış ve birkaç adı geçen uzmanın yer aldığı bir rapordur. Doğa ve çevre en sık konulardır. Karttaki araştırma fiillerini öğren: kimin görüşünü okuduğunu söylerler.","fa":"Passage 2 اغلب گزارشی درباره‌ی یک مسئله‌ی علمی است، با بخش‌های حرف‌دار و چند کارشناسِ نام‌برده. طبیعت و محیط زیست رایج‌ترین موضوع‌ها هستند. فعل‌های پژوهشیِ کارت را یاد بگیر: می‌گویند نظرِ چه کسی را می‌خوانی."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x05-r2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-research","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Bringing a lost plant back","tr":"Kaybolan bir bitkiyi geri getirmek","fa":"برگرداندن یک گیاهِ ازدست‌رفته"},"asks":{"en":"A report in seven lettered sections about a rare plant: why it declined, how scientists identify and grow it, why it matters. Three researchers give their views, and you match each statement to one of them.","tr":"Nadir bir bitki hakkında harflerle ayrılmış yedi bölümlük bir rapor: neden azaldığı, bilim insanlarının onu nasıl tanıyıp yetiştirdiği, neden önemli olduğu. Üç araştırmacı görüşlerini veriyor ve sen her ifadeyi birine eşleştiriyorsun.","fa":"گزارشی در هفت بخشِ حرف‌دار درباره‌ی یک گیاه کمیاب: چرا کم شد، دانشمندها چطور آن را تشخیص می‌دهند و پرورش می‌دهند، چرا مهم است. سه پژوهشگر نظرشان را می‌گویند و تو هر جمله را به یکی‌شان وصل می‌کنی."},"fields":["Causes of decline","Mixing with other plants","How to identify it","How to grow it","Value for wildlife","Value for people","Three researchers"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"became rare / quietly disappeared","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"cleared","b":"cut down for farming","tr":"açıldı, temizlendi","fa":"پاک‌سازی شد"},{"a":"pollinate","b":"carry pollen from flower to flower","tr":"tozlaştırmak","fa":"گرده‌افشانی کردن"},{"a":"hybrid","b":"a mix of two kinds / a cross","tr":"melez","fa":"دورگه"},{"a":"identify","b":"tell which is which / recognise","tr":"tanımlamak, ayırt etmek","fa":"تشخیص دادن"},{"a":"reliable","b":"you can trust it / will settle the matter","tr":"güvenilir","fa":"قابل اعتماد"},{"a":"genetically identical","b":"an exact copy of its parent","tr":"genetik olarak aynı","fa":"از نظر ژنتیکی یکسان"},{"a":"resistance","b":"protection against disease","tr":"direnç","fa":"مقاومت"},{"a":"a wide range of","b":"a wider variety of / many kinds of","tr":"çok çeşitli","fa":"طیف گسترده‌ای از"},{"a":"cautious","b":"careful / should not promise more than we know","tr":"temkinli","fa":"محتاط"},{"a":"suggests","b":"believes / points out / warns","tr":"öne sürüyor","fa":"مطرح می‌کند"},{"a":"a third","b":"roughly one in three","tr":"üçte bir","fa":"یک‌سوم"}],"traps":[{"en":"Whose view? \"Some have suggested...\" is not the researcher’s own view. In section G the idea is other people’s; the named researcher is cautious about it.","tr":"Kimin görüşü? \"Bazıları öne sürdü...\" araştırmacının kendi görüşü değildir. Bir bölümde fikir başkalarına ait olabilir; adı geçen araştırmacı ona temkinli yaklaşabilir.","fa":"نظرِ چه کسی؟ «بعضی‌ها مطرح کرده‌اند...» نظر خودِ پژوهشگر نیست. ممکن است ایده مال دیگران باشد و پژوهشگرِ نام‌برده درباره‌اش محتاط باشد."},{"en":"Which section: a section may mention a word from the question in passing. Choose the section where the whole idea is, not just the word.","tr":"Hangi bölüm: bir bölüm sorudaki bir kelimeyi geçerken anabilir. Yalnızca kelimenin değil, fikrin tamamının olduğu bölümü seç.","fa":"کدام بخش: ممکن است بخشی کلمه‌ای از سؤال را گذرا بیاورد. بخشی را انتخاب کن که کل ایده در آن است، نه فقط آن کلمه."},{"en":"Summary from the passage: copy one word in the form the passage uses: plural if the passage says gardens.","tr":"Metinden özet: kelimeyi metindeki biçimiyle kopyala; metin gardens diyorsa çoğul.","fa":"خلاصه از روی متن: کلمه را به همان شکلی که در متن آمده کپی کن؛ اگر متن gardens می‌گوید، جمع."}],"example":{"text":"\"Several farmers believe the new seeds are tougher. The plant scientist Ana Ruiz is less sure: ‘The early results look good, but one dry summer proves nothing.’\"","item":"Statement: The evidence so far is not enough to judge the new seeds. Who says this?","answer":"Ana Ruiz","why":{"en":"The farmers believe the seeds are tougher; Ruiz says one summer \"proves nothing\" = not enough evidence.","tr":"Çiftçiler tohumların daha dayanıklı olduğuna inanıyor; Ruiz bir yazın \"hiçbir şey kanıtlamadığını\" söylüyor = yeterli kanıt yok.","fa":"کشاورزها معتقدند بذرها مقاوم‌ترند؛ رویز می‌گوید یک تابستان «هیچ چیزی را ثابت نمی‌کند» یعنی شواهد کافی نیست."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-report","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Reports on ecosystems and the environment","tr":"Ekosistemler ve çevre üzerine raporlar","fa":"گزارش درباره‌ی زیست‌بوم‌ها و محیط زیست"},"asks":{"en":"A report in lettered paragraphs about an ecosystem or an environmental problem: what it is, why it matters, what threatens it and what is being done. Headings name each paragraph’s main idea; matching information asks where one detail is.","tr":"Bir ekosistem ya da çevre sorunu hakkında harfli paragraflardan oluşan bir rapor: ne olduğu, neden önemli olduğu, onu neyin tehdit ettiği ve neler yapıldığı. Başlıklar her paragrafın ana fikrini adlandırır; bilgi eşleştirme tek bir ayrıntının nerede olduğunu sorar.","fa":"گزارشی با پاراگراف‌های حرف‌دار درباره‌ی یک زیست‌بوم یا یک مشکل محیط‌زیستی: چیست، چرا مهم است، چه چیزی تهدیدش می‌کند و چه کاری انجام می‌شود. عنوان‌ها ایده‌ی اصلی هر پاراگراف‌اند؛ جورکردن اطلاعات می‌پرسد یک نکته‌ی جزئی کجاست."},"fields":["The economic value of the forest","An unexpected benefit","Causes of decline","Early attempts at protection","A way of measuring change","Which paragraph mentions a comparison with another region?"],"words":[{"a":"a threat to","b":"puts at risk / endangers","tr":"... için tehdit","fa":"تهدیدی برای"},{"a":"causes","b":"the reasons / what led to","tr":"nedenler","fa":"علت‌ها"},{"a":"an unexpected benefit","b":"a surprising advantage","tr":"beklenmedik bir fayda","fa":"فایده‌ای غیرمنتظره"},{"a":"economic value","b":"worth money / income from","tr":"ekonomik değer","fa":"ارزش اقتصادی"},{"a":"early attempts","b":"the first efforts / initially tried","tr":"ilk girişimler","fa":"تلاش‌های اولیه"},{"a":"a new approach","b":"a different method / instead, now","tr":"yeni bir yaklaşım","fa":"رویکردی تازه"},{"a":"measuring","b":"monitoring / recording","tr":"ölçme","fa":"اندازه‌گیری"},{"a":"restore","b":"bring back / replant","tr":"eski haline getirmek","fa":"احیا کردن"},{"a":"long-term","b":"over decades / in the future","tr":"uzun vadeli","fa":"بلندمدت"},{"a":"local communities","b":"people living nearby","tr":"yerel halk","fa":"جوامع محلی"},{"a":"a comparison","b":"unlike / whereas in","tr":"bir karşılaştırma","fa":"یک مقایسه"},{"a":"consequences","b":"effects / results","tr":"sonuçlar","fa":"پیامدها"}],"traps":[{"en":"The detail trap: one heading matches a single detail of the paragraph, not its main idea.","tr":"Ayrıntı tuzağı: bir başlık paragrafın ana fikrine değil, tek bir ayrıntısına uyar.","fa":"دام جزئیات: یک عنوان با یک نکته‌ی جزئیِ پاراگراف جور است، نه با ایده‌ی اصلی‌اش."},{"en":"Matching information: the detail may sit in a paragraph whose main idea is something else.","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirme: ayrıntı, ana fikri başka bir şey olan bir paragrafta olabilir.","fa":"جورکردن اطلاعات: جزئیات ممکن است در پاراگرافی باشد که ایده‌ی اصلی‌اش چیز دیگری است."}],"example":{"text":"D  Restoring peat bogs was once thought to be simple: block the drains and wait for the water to return. Yet in many early projects the peat stayed dry for years, because the bogs had sunk below the level of the land around them.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph D:  i  Why early restoration often failed   ii  The value of peat for farming   iii  How drains are built","answer":"i","why":{"en":"\"Once thought to be simple... yet... stayed dry\" = early attempts that failed. Drains are only a detail.","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar basit sanılıyordu... ama... kuru kaldı\" = başarısız ilk girişimler. Kanallar yalnızca bir ayrıntı.","fa":"«زمانی ساده تصور می‌شد... ولی... خشک ماند» = تلاش‌های اولیه‌ی ناموفق. زهکش‌ها فقط یک نکته‌ی جزئی‌اند."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three tasks on one passage","tr":"Bir metin üzerinde üç görev","fa":"سه تمرین روی یک متن"},"body":{"en":"Questions 14-18: which section, A-G, contains each piece of information? Letters can be used more than once. Questions 19-23: match each statement with a researcher, A, B or C. Questions 24-26: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage.","tr":"Soru 14-18: her bilgi A-G’den hangi bölümde? Harfler birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 19-23: her ifadeyi bir araştırmacıyla eşleştir: A, B ya da C. Soru 24-26: bir özeti metinden ONE WORD ONLY ile tamamla.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۴ تا ۱۸: هر اطلاعات در کدام بخش، A تا G، است؟ حرف‌ها می‌توانند بیش از یک بار بیایند. سؤال‌های ۱۹ تا ۲۳: هر جمله را به یک پژوهشگر، A، B یا C، وصل کن. سؤال‌های ۲۴ تا ۲۶: یک خلاصه را با ONE WORD ONLY از متن کامل کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Do the people first","tr":"Önce kişileri yap","fa":"اول سراغ آدم‌ها برو"},"steps":[{"en":"Circle every researcher’s name in the passage. Each may appear in more than one section.","tr":"Metindeki her araştırmacının adını daire içine al. Her biri birden fazla bölümde geçebilir.","fa":"دور اسم هر پژوهشگر در متن خط بکش. هر کدام ممکن است در بیش از یک بخش بیاید."},{"en":"Read what each person says or thinks, and match the meaning of the statement, not its words.","tr":"Her kişinin ne söylediğini ya da düşündüğünü oku; ifadenin kelimelerini değil anlamını eşleştir.","fa":"بخوان هر نفر چه می‌گوید یا چه فکر می‌کند و معنی جمله را جور کن، نه کلمه‌هایش را."},{"en":"For \"which section\", the information is usually one detail: an example, a figure, a description. Look for it inside the paragraph, not in its topic sentence.","tr":"\"Hangi bölüm\" sorularında bilgi genelde tek bir ayrıntıdır: bir örnek, bir rakam, bir betimleme. Onu paragrafın konu cümlesinde değil, içinde ara.","fa":"در «کدام بخش»، اطلاعات معمولاً یک جزئیات است: یک مثال، یک عدد، یک توصیف. آن را درون پاراگراف بگرد، نه در جمله‌ی اصلی‌اش."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Reported views","tr":"Aktarılan görüşler","fa":"نظرهای نقل‌شده"},"body":{"en":"A section can contain an idea that a researcher reports but does not share: \"Some have suggested... X is cautious.\" Match the statement to the person whose own view it is. If nobody named holds the view, it does not belong to any of them.","tr":"Bir bölümde bir araştırmacının aktardığı ama paylaşmadığı bir fikir olabilir: \"Bazıları öne sürdü... X temkinli.\" İfadeyi, görüş kimin kendi görüşüyse o kişiyle eşleştir. Adı geçen hiç kimse bu görüşte değilse, hiçbirine ait değildir.","fa":"ممکن است در یک بخش ایده‌ای باشد که پژوهشگر نقلش می‌کند ولی قبولش ندارد: «بعضی‌ها مطرح کرده‌اند... X محتاط است». جمله را به کسی وصل کن که نظرِ خودش است. اگر هیچ‌کدام از آدم‌های نام‌برده این نظر را ندارند، مال هیچ‌کدامشان نیست."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"Matching a researcher, step by step","tr":"Bir araştırmacıyı eşleştirmek, adım adım","fa":"وصل کردن یک پژوهشگر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Match each statement with the correct researcher.","text":"\"Local fishermen say the river is cleaner than ever. Dr Okafor agrees that the water looks clear, but she warns that clear water can still carry high levels of chemicals.\"","item":"Statement: Water that looks clean may not be safe. A the fishermen  B Dr Okafor","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"Find both views: the fishermen say \"cleaner than ever\"; Okafor \"agrees... but she warns\".","tr":"İki görüşü bul: balıkçılar \"hiç olmadığı kadar temiz\" diyor; Okafor \"katılıyor... ama uyarıyor\".","fa":"هر دو نظر را پیدا کن: ماهیگیرها می‌گویند «تمیزتر از همیشه»؛ اوکافور «موافق است... اما هشدار می‌دهد»."},{"en":"The statement is about danger in clean-looking water: that is the warning.","tr":"İfade temiz görünen sudaki tehlikeyle ilgili: bu, uyarının kendisi.","fa":"جمله درباره‌ی خطر در آبی است که تمیز به نظر می‌رسد: یعنی همان هشدار."},{"en":"\"Can still carry high levels of chemicals\" = may not be safe: B.","tr":"\"Hâlâ yüksek düzeyde kimyasal taşıyabilir\" = güvenli olmayabilir: B.","fa":"«هنوز ممکن است مقدار زیادی مواد شیمیایی داشته باشد» یعنی شاید سالم نباشد: B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"Some engineers claim the bridge will last 200 years. Professor Lind thinks this is optimistic.\" Whose view is \"The bridge may not last as long as people say\"?","options":["Professor Lind","the engineers","both"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The engineers make the claim; Lind calls it \"optimistic\", which means she doubts it.","tr":"Mühendisler iddiayı ortaya atıyor; Lind ona \"iyimser\" diyor, yani şüpheli.","fa":"مهندس‌ها ادعا می‌کنند؛ لیند آن را «خوش‌بینانه» می‌داند، یعنی به آن شک دارد."}},"remember":{"en":"Circle the names first, match meanings not words, and check whose view each idea really is.","tr":"Önce isimleri daire içine al, kelimeleri değil anlamları eşleştir ve her fikrin gerçekte kimin görüşü olduğuna bak.","fa":"اول دور اسم‌ها خط بکش، معنی‌ها را جور کن نه کلمه‌ها را، و ببین هر ایده واقعاً نظرِ کیست."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x05-r2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 2","title":{"en":"Bringing back the wild apple","tr":"Yabani elmayı geri getirmek","fa":"برگرداندن سیب وحشی"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.","passage":"Bringing back the wild apple\n\nA  Long before orchards existed, Europe's woods contained a small, thorny tree whose hard, sour fruit few people would choose to eat today. The European wild apple, often called the crab apple, was once found from Spain to Russia, and it played a part in the history of the sweet apples we buy in shops. Yet in many regions it has quietly become one of the rarest trees in the countryside. A growing number of conservation projects are now trying to bring it back, and their work has turned out to be far more complicated than simply planting trees.\n\nB  The first reason for the decline is obvious: over centuries, most of the woodland where the wild apple grew was cleared for farming. The second is less obvious and concerns the way the tree reproduces. Wild apples do not grow in groves. They tend to stand alone, often hundreds of metres from their nearest neighbour. Since a tree cannot fertilise its own flowers, it depends on bees and other insects to bring pollen from another apple tree. When the nearest wild tree is far away, the pollen that arrives often comes from a garden or an orchard instead. In a landscape full of villages, where almost every back garden has an apple tree, the odds are heavily against two wild trees ever meeting.\n\nC  The result is a slow mixing of wild and cultivated apples. The seeds of a wild tree pollinated in this way grow into hybrids, which may look almost exactly like their wild parent. \"A tree that looks perfectly wild may have a domestic grandparent,\" says the geneticist Mirela Constantin, who has spent ten years sampling trees across central Europe. When her team tested trees that had been recorded as wild in one national survey, they found that roughly a third of them were in fact hybrids. In some lowland areas close to villages, the proportion was much higher.\n\nD  This raises a practical question: how do you know a wild apple when you see one? Field guides list several features, including thorns on the branches, leaves that lose their hairs as they mature, and fruit less than three centimetres across. However, the botanist Hamish Tolland warns that \"no single feature, and not even a combination of them, will settle the matter\". Hybrids can have thorns, and true wild trees can produce surprisingly large fruit in a good year. For this reason, Tolland's group has built a database of genetic profiles, so that a small piece of leaf can be compared with hundreds of confirmed wild trees.\n\nE  Once pure trees have been identified, the next step is to grow more of them. Growing trees from seed is cheap, but because of the pollination problem, there is no guarantee that the seedlings will be pure. Most projects therefore rely on grafting: a cutting is taken from a confirmed wild tree and joined to a young rootstock, so that the new tree is genetically identical to its parent. Some projects go further and create seed orchards, in which only tested wild trees are planted, well away from gardens. The ecologist Yuki Arai believes that new trees should always be planted in groups. \"A single tree in a field may look romantic,\" she says, \"but it will simply repeat the problem we are trying to solve.\"\n\nF  Why does any of this matter? Part of the answer is wildlife. The wild apple blossoms early in spring, when few other flowers are open, and provides food for bees that have just come out of hibernation. Tolland points out that it supports a wider variety of insects than most other small trees in the same woods. In autumn, the fallen fruit is eaten by birds, deer and badgers, which then carry the seeds away and leave them in their droppings, often far from the parent tree. In this way, the fruit that people find too sour to eat does exactly the job it evolved to do.\n\nG  There may also be value for people. Commercial apples are prone to a number of diseases, and breeders are always looking for new sources of resistance. Some have suggested that wild apples, which have survived for thousands of years without any help, carry genes that could protect cultivated varieties. Arai is cautious. \"It is a reasonable idea,\" she says, \"but so far the research is at a very early stage, and we should not promise farmers more than we know.\" For now, the main aim of most projects is simply to make sure that, a century from now, a walk in the woods can still include a wild apple in blossom.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 14-18. Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"questions":[{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"an explanation of why wild trees are seldom pollinated by each other","correct":1,"evidence":"They tend to stand alone, often hundreds of metres from their nearest neighbour","why":{"en":"B: wild apples \"stand alone\", so the pollen that arrives often comes from a garden instead.","tr":"B: yabani elmalar \"tek başına duruyor\", bu yüzden gelen polen çoğu zaman bir bahçeden geliyor.","fa":"B: سیب‌های وحشی «تک‌تک ایستاده‌اند»، پس گرده‌ای که می‌رسد اغلب از یک باغچه می‌آید."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":15,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to animals carrying seeds to new places","correct":5,"evidence":"which then carry the seeds away and leave them in their droppings","why":{"en":"F: birds, deer and badgers eat the fruit and \"carry the seeds away\".","tr":"F: kuşlar, geyikler ve porsuklar meyveyi yiyip \"tohumları uzağa taşıyor\".","fa":"F: پرنده‌ها، گوزن‌ها و گورکن‌ها میوه را می‌خورند و «بذرها را با خود می‌برند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":16,"kind":"match","prompt":"a description of features that are used to identify wild trees","correct":3,"evidence":"thorns on the branches, leaves that lose their hairs as they mature","why":{"en":"D lists the features: thorns, leaves, small fruit. Section C mentions identification by testing, not by features.","tr":"D özellikleri sıralıyor: dikenler, yapraklar, küçük meyve. C bölümü özelliklerle değil, testle tanımadan söz ediyor.","fa":"D ویژگی‌ها را فهرست می‌کند: خار، برگ، میوه‌ی کوچک. بخش C از تشخیص با آزمایش حرف می‌زند، نه با ویژگی‌ها."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":17,"kind":"match","prompt":"a possible benefit for people who grow apples commercially","correct":6,"evidence":"carry genes that could protect cultivated varieties","why":{"en":"G: wild genes \"could protect cultivated varieties\" from disease.","tr":"G: yabani genler kültür çeşitlerini hastalıktan \"koruyabilir\".","fa":"G: ژن‌های وحشی «می‌توانند از گونه‌های پرورشی محافظت کنند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":18,"kind":"match","prompt":"a figure showing how many trees recorded as wild were not pure","correct":2,"evidence":"roughly a third of them were in fact hybrids","why":{"en":"C: \"roughly a third of them were in fact hybrids\".","tr":"C: \"yaklaşık üçte biri aslında melezdi\".","fa":"C: «تقریباً یک‌سومشان در واقع دورگه بودند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 19-23. Look at the following statements (Questions 19-23) and the list of researchers below. Match each statement with the correct researcher, A, B or C. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Mirela Constantin","B Hamish Tolland","C Yuki Arai"],"questions":[{"n":19,"kind":"match","prompt":"The appearance of a tree is not enough to show whether it is wild.","correct":1,"evidence":"not even a combination of them, will settle the matter","why":{"en":"Tolland: \"no single feature, and not even a combination of them, will settle the matter\".","tr":"Tolland: \"tek bir özellik, hatta bunların birleşimi bile meseleyi çözmez\".","fa":"تولند: «هیچ ویژگی‌ای به‌تنهایی، و حتی ترکیبی از آن‌ها، مسئله را حل نمی‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"match","prompt":"New trees should not be planted on their own.","correct":2,"evidence":"new trees should always be planted in groups","why":{"en":"Arai: trees \"should always be planted in groups\"; a single tree \"will simply repeat the problem\".","tr":"Arai: ağaçlar \"her zaman gruplar hâlinde dikilmeli\"; tek bir ağaç \"sorunu tekrarlar\".","fa":"آرای: درخت‌ها «باید همیشه گروهی کاشته شوند»؛ یک درختِ تنها «فقط مشکل را تکرار می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":21,"kind":"match","prompt":"A tree may look wild even though one of its ancestors was cultivated.","correct":0,"evidence":"may have a domestic grandparent","why":{"en":"Constantin: a wild-looking tree \"may have a domestic grandparent\".","tr":"Constantin: yabani görünen bir ağacın \"evcil bir büyükebeveyni olabilir\".","fa":"کنستانتین: درختی که وحشی به نظر می‌رسد «ممکن است پدربزرگ یا مادربزرگی پرورشی داشته باشد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":22,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is too early to say whether wild trees can help protect commercial apples from disease.","correct":2,"evidence":"the research is at a very early stage","why":{"en":"\"Some have suggested\" the idea; Arai’s own view is that \"the research is at a very early stage\".","tr":"Fikri \"bazıları öne sürdü\"; Arai’nin kendi görüşü \"araştırmanın çok erken bir aşamada\" olduğu.","fa":"ایده را «بعضی‌ها مطرح کرده‌اند»؛ نظرِ خودِ آرای این است که «پژوهش در مرحله‌ی خیلی اولیه است»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":23,"kind":"match","prompt":"The wild apple is home to more kinds of insect than many similar trees.","correct":1,"evidence":"it supports a wider variety of insects than most other small trees","why":{"en":"Tolland \"points out that it supports a wider variety of insects than most other small trees\".","tr":"Tolland \"çoğu küçük ağaçtan daha çeşitli böceği beslediğini\" belirtiyor.","fa":"تولند «اشاره می‌کند که از بیشترِ درخت‌های کوچک دیگر، انواع بیشتری از حشره‌ها را پشتیبانی می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 24-26. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"Growing new wild apple trees","questions":[{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Because seedlings may not be pure, most projects use ___,","accept":[["grafting"]],"limit":1,"evidence":"Most projects therefore rely on grafting","why":{"en":"\"Most projects therefore rely on grafting\": use = rely on.","tr":"\"Bu yüzden çoğu proje aşılamaya dayanıyor\": use = rely on.","fa":"«به همین دلیل بیشتر پروژه‌ها به پیوند زدن تکیه می‌کنند»: use یعنی rely on."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"in which a cutting from a wild tree is joined to a young ___.","accept":[["rootstock"]],"limit":1,"evidence":"joined to a young rootstock","why":{"en":"\"A cutting is taken from a confirmed wild tree and joined to a young rootstock.\"","tr":"\"Doğrulanmış yabani bir ağaçtan bir çelik alınıp genç bir anaca bağlanıyor.\"","fa":"«یک قلمه از درخت وحشیِ تأییدشده گرفته و به یک پایه‌ی جوان پیوند زده می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Seed orchards contain only tested trees and are placed well away from ___.","accept":[["gardens"]],"limit":1,"evidence":"well away from gardens","why":{"en":"\"Planted, well away from gardens\". Copy the plural.","tr":"\"Bahçelerden epey uzağa dikiliyor\". Çoğulu kopyala.","fa":"«دور از باغچه‌ها کاشته می‌شوند». جمع را کپی کن."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x05-r2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"A statement says \"X doubts the claim\". Which words in a passage show this?","options":["X points out that the claim is well known","X has tested the claim for ten years","X is cautious: \"we should not promise more than we know\""],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Being cautious and warning against promises = doubting the claim.","tr":"Temkinli olmak ve söz vermemeyi öğütlemek = iddiadan şüphe etmek.","fa":"محتاط بودن و هشدار دادن درباره‌ی قول‌ها یعنی شک داشتن به ادعا."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Most of the hybrids grew near villages.\" A hybrid is...","options":["a very old tree","a mix of two different kinds","a tree grown in a pot"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A hybrid comes from two different kinds of parent.","tr":"Melez, iki farklı türden ebeveynden gelir.","fa":"دورگه از دو والدِ نوعِ متفاوت به وجود می‌آید."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A researcher’s name appears in sections D and F. What do you do before matching a statement to her?","options":["Read what she says in both sections","Read only the first section","Read only the last paragraph"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The statement may match either mention; read both.","tr":"İfade iki anıştan birine uyabilir; ikisini de oku.","fa":"جمله ممکن است با هر کدام از دو جا جور باشد؛ هر دو را بخوان."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Many gardeners say the plant is easy to grow. Dr Field has found it hard to keep alive.\" Whose view is \"The plant is difficult to grow\"?","options":["the gardeners","both","Dr Field"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The gardeners say it is easy; only Dr Field finds it hard.","tr":"Bahçıvanlar kolay diyor; yalnızca Dr Field zor buluyor.","fa":"باغبان‌ها می‌گویند آسان است؛ فقط دکتر فیلد آن را سخت می‌داند."}}],"id":"c-x05-r2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r2"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 2: advice for work","tr":"GT Reading Section 2: iş için tavsiyeler","fa":"GT Reading Section 2: توصیه‌هایی برای کار"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete sentences and notes with one word from two work-related texts, keeping to the word limit and the exact form of the word.","tr":"Bu derste işle ilgili iki metinden tek bir kelimeyle cümleleri ve notları tamamlamayı, kelime sınırına ve kelimenin tam biçimine uymayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه از دو متن کاری کامل کنی و سقف کلمه و شکل دقیق کلمه را رعایت کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: meetings and a new shop","tr":"Bu sınav: toplantılar ve yeni bir dükkân","fa":"این آزمون: جلسه‌ها و یک مغازه‌ی تازه"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 2 is always about work: job adverts, workplace rules, or advice on running a team or a business. Here both texts are advice. The questions follow each text in order.","tr":"GT Section 2 her zaman işle ilgilidir: iş ilanları, işyeri kuralları ya da bir ekibi veya işletmeyi yönetme tavsiyeleri. Burada iki metin de tavsiye. Sorular her metni sırayla izler.","fa":"GT Section 2 همیشه درباره‌ی کار است: آگهی استخدام، قانون‌های محل کار یا توصیه برای اداره‌ی تیم یا کسب‌وکار. این‌جا هر دو متن توصیه‌اند. سؤال‌ها هر متن را به ترتیب دنبال می‌کنند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x05-r2gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT2-business"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-business","n":16,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 16 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 16’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۶ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Running meetings and a small shop","tr":"Toplantı ve küçük bir dükkân yönetmek","fa":"اداره‌ی جلسه و یک مغازه‌ی کوچک"},"asks":{"en":"Two texts of practical advice for work: how a new supervisor should run team meetings, and how to give a new shop the best chance. You complete sentences and notes with one word from each text.","tr":"İş için pratik tavsiyeler içeren iki metin: yeni bir amirin ekip toplantılarını nasıl yönetmesi gerektiği ve yeni bir dükkâna en iyi şansın nasıl verileceği. Her metinden bir kelimeyle cümleleri ve notları tamamlarsın.","fa":"دو متن با توصیه‌های عملی برای کار: یک سرپرست تازه‌کار چطور جلسه‌های تیم را اداره کند و چطور به یک مغازه‌ی تازه بهترین شانس را بدهی. جمله‌ها و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه از هر متن کامل می‌کنی."},"fields":["Before","During","After","Location","Money","Stock","Customers","Help"],"words":[{"a":"agenda","b":"a list of topics for a meeting","tr":"gündem","fa":"دستور جلسه"},{"a":"minutes","b":"the written record of a meeting","tr":"toplantı tutanağı","fa":"صورت‌جلسه"},{"a":"concentration","b":"attention / focus","tr":"dikkat, konsantrasyon","fa":"تمرکز"},{"a":"dominate","b":"talk the most / take over","tr":"baskın olmak","fa":"غالب شدن، میدان‌داری کردن"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"whose job it is","tr":"... den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"lease","b":"a contract to rent a building","tr":"kira sözleşmesi","fa":"قرارداد اجاره"},{"a":"footfall","b":"the number of people who walk past","tr":"yaya trafiği","fa":"تعداد رهگذرها"},{"a":"expenses","b":"costs / money you have to pay out","tr":"giderler","fa":"هزینه‌ها"},{"a":"stock","b":"the goods a shop has to sell","tr":"stok, mal","fa":"موجودی کالا"},{"a":"ties up money","b":"money you cannot use for anything else","tr":"parayı bağlar","fa":"پول را قفل می‌کند"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"at no cost / free","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"regular customers","b":"loyal customers / people who come back","tr":"sürekli müşteriler","fa":"مشتری‌های همیشگی"}],"traps":[{"en":"The word limit is ONE WORD ONLY: \"a brief report\" is three words. The gap already has \"a\" or an adjective printed before it.","tr":"Kelime sınırı ONE WORD ONLY: \"a brief report\" üç kelime. Boşluğun önünde \"a\" ya da bir sıfat zaten yazılı.","fa":"سقف کلمه ONE WORD ONLY است: «a brief report» سه کلمه است. قبل از جای خالی «a» یا یک صفت از قبل چاپ شده."},{"en":"Plural or singular: copy the form the text uses. If the text says \"the minutes\", the note needs minutes, not minute.","tr":"Çoğul ya da tekil: metnin kullandığı biçimi kopyala. Metin \"the minutes\" diyorsa not minute değil minutes ister.","fa":"جمع یا مفرد: همان شکلی را که متن به کار برده کپی کن. اگر متن «the minutes» می‌گوید، یادداشت minutes می‌خواهد، نه minute."}],"example":{"text":"\"New staff are paired with an experienced colleague, known as a mentor, for their first month.\"","item":"Sentence: For the first month, new staff work with a ___.","answer":"mentor","why":{"en":"\"An experienced colleague, known as a mentor\": one word from the text fits the gap.","tr":"\"Mentor olarak bilinen deneyimli bir iş arkadaşı\": metinden tek bir kelime boşluğa uyuyor.","fa":"«یک همکار باتجربه که به او mentor می‌گویند»: یک کلمه از متن در جای خالی جا می‌شود."}}},{"id":"GT2-business","ctx":["GT2-business"],"title":{"en":"Running a team or a small business","tr":"Bir ekibi ya da küçük bir işletmeyi yönetmek","fa":"اداره‌ی یک تیم یا یک کسب‌وکار کوچک"},"asks":{"en":"Workplace guides on meetings, projects, delegation, marketing, flexible working or types of training. Sentence and note completion test the advice and the steps.","tr":"Toplantılar, projeler, görev devri, pazarlama, esnek çalışma ya da eğitim türleri üzerine iş yeri rehberleri. Cümle ve not tamamlama tavsiyeleri ve adımları sınar.","fa":"راهنماهای محیط کار درباره‌ی جلسه، پروژه، واگذاری کار، بازاریابی، کار منعطف یا انواع آموزش. کامل کردن جمله و یادداشت توصیه‌ها و مرحله‌ها را می‌سنجد."},"fields":["Before a meeting, send the ___ to everyone.","Give tasks to staff who can do them ___.","Flexible hours must be agreed with your ___.","Training: on the job · external course · online"],"words":[{"a":"agenda","b":"list of points for the meeting","tr":"gündem","fa":"دستور جلسه"},{"a":"delegate","b":"give a task to someone else","tr":"görev devretmek","fa":"واگذار کردن"},{"a":"deadline","b":"the date it must be done by","tr":"son tarih","fa":"مهلت"},{"a":"budget","b":"the money available","tr":"bütçe","fa":"بودجه"},{"a":"priorities","b":"what matters most","tr":"öncelikler","fa":"اولویت‌ها"},{"a":"minutes","b":"written record of a meeting","tr":"toplantı tutanağı","fa":"صورت‌جلسه"},{"a":"colleague","b":"co-worker","tr":"iş arkadaşı","fa":"همکار"},{"a":"line manager","b":"the person you report to","tr":"bağlı olduğun yönetici","fa":"مدیر مستقیم"},{"a":"flexible hours","b":"choose when you start and finish","tr":"esnek çalışma saatleri","fa":"ساعت کاری منعطف"},{"a":"client","b":"customer","tr":"müşteri","fa":"مشتری"},{"a":"promote","b":"advertise / market","tr":"tanıtmak","fa":"تبلیغ کردن"},{"a":"progress","b":"how far the work has got","tr":"ilerleme","fa":"پیشرفت"}],"traps":[{"en":"The sentence to complete is a paraphrase; the gap word is copied from the text.","tr":"Tamamlanacak cümle başka sözcüklerle yazılmıştır; boşluktaki kelime metinden kopyalanır.","fa":"جمله‌ای که کامل می‌کنی با کلمه‌های دیگر نوشته شده؛ کلمه‌ی جای خالی از متن کپی می‌شود."},{"en":"Lists of advice: the question asks about one step (\"before the meeting\"); the text lists several.","tr":"Tavsiye listeleri: soru tek bir adımı sorar (\"toplantıdan önce\"); metin birkaçını sıralar.","fa":"فهرست توصیه‌ها: سؤال درباره‌ی یک مرحله است («قبل از جلسه»)؛ متن چند مرحله را می‌شمارد."}],"example":{"text":"Circulate the minutes within 24 hours, while decisions are still fresh. Each action point should name one person, not a whole department.","item":"Sentence: Each action point should name a single ___.   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"person","why":{"en":"\"Name one person, not a whole department\": a single person.","tr":"\"Bütün bir bölümü değil, tek bir kişiyi yaz\": a single person.","fa":"«یک نفر را نام ببر، نه کل یک بخش را»: a single person."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-business"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-business","n":16,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 16 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 16’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۶ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Sentences, then notes","tr":"Önce cümleler, sonra notlar","fa":"اول جمله‌ها، بعد یادداشت‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Questions 15-21: complete sentences about the first text. Questions 22-27: complete notes about the second text. Both use ONE WORD ONLY from the text. The headings in the text match the order of the questions.","tr":"Soru 15-21: ilk metinle ilgili cümleleri tamamla. Soru 22-27: ikinci metinle ilgili notları tamamla. İkisinde de metinden ONE WORD ONLY kullanılır. Metindeki başlıklar soruların sırasına uyar.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۵ تا ۲۱: جمله‌هایی درباره‌ی متن اول را کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۲۲ تا ۲۷: یادداشت‌هایی درباره‌ی متن دوم را کامل کن. در هر دو فقط ONE WORD ONLY از متن. عنوان‌های متن با ترتیب سؤال‌ها جورند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Grammar tells you the word","tr":"Dil bilgisi kelimeyi söyler","fa":"دستور زبان کلمه را می‌گوید"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the sentence and decide what the gap needs: a noun after \"an\", an adjective before a noun, a plural after \"the\".","tr":"Cümleyi oku ve boşluğun neye ihtiyacı olduğuna karar ver: \"an\"den sonra isim, isimden önce sıfat, \"the\"den sonra çoğul.","fa":"جمله را بخوان و تصمیم بگیر جای خالی چه می‌خواهد: بعد از «an» اسم، قبل از اسم صفت، بعد از «the» جمع."},{"en":"Use the headings in the text to find the right part, then look for a paraphrase of the sentence.","tr":"Doğru kısmı bulmak için metindeki başlıkları kullan, sonra cümlenin başka sözcüklerle söylenişini ara.","fa":"با کمک عنوان‌های متن بخش درست را پیدا کن و بعد دنبال بیانِ دیگری از همان جمله بگرد."},{"en":"Copy one word exactly, with its spelling and its plural ending.","tr":"Tek bir kelimeyi yazımı ve çoğul ekiyle aynen kopyala.","fa":"یک کلمه را دقیقاً با املا و نشانه‌ی جمعش کپی کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Too many words","tr":"Fazla kelime","fa":"کلمه‌ی زیادی"},"body":{"en":"The right idea in two words is wrong when the limit is one. The sentence is written so that one word fits: the article or the adjective is already there. Read the words just before and just after the gap.","tr":"Sınır bir kelimeyken iki kelimelik doğru fikir yanlıştır. Cümle, tek bir kelime uyacak biçimde yazılmıştır: tanımlık ya da sıfat zaten oradadır. Boşluğun hemen önündeki ve arkasındaki kelimeleri oku.","fa":"وقتی سقف یک کلمه است، ایده‌ی درست با دو کلمه غلط است. جمله طوری نوشته شده که یک کلمه در آن جا شود: حرف تعریف یا صفت از قبل هست. کلمه‌های درست قبل و بعد از جای خالی را بخوان."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One sentence, step by step","tr":"Bir cümle, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the sentence below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","text":"\"Uniforms are washed by the company, but staff must keep their own safety boots clean.\"","item":"Staff are responsible for cleaning their ___.","answer":"boots","walk":[{"en":"The gap follows \"their\", so it needs a noun.","tr":"Boşluk \"their\"den sonra geliyor, yani bir isim gerekiyor.","fa":"جای خالی بعد از «their» است، پس اسم می‌خواهد."},{"en":"\"Responsible for cleaning\" = must keep clean. The uniforms are washed by the company, so they are not the answer.","tr":"\"Temizlemekten sorumlu\" = temiz tutmak zorunda. Üniformaları şirket yıkıyor, yani cevap onlar değil.","fa":"«مسئول تمیز کردن» یعنی باید تمیز نگه دارد. یونیفرم‌ها را شرکت می‌شوید، پس جواب نیستند."},{"en":"\"safety boots\" is two words; one word is allowed, so write boots.","tr":"\"safety boots\" iki kelime; bir kelimeye izin var, o yüzden boots yaz.","fa":"«safety boots» دو کلمه است؛ یک کلمه مجاز است، پس boots را بنویس."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Staff receive a written contract within two weeks.\" Sentence: \"A written ___ is given within two weeks.\" (ONE WORD ONLY)","options":["written contract","contract","contracts"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"written\" is printed, and the text uses the singular: contract.","tr":"\"written\" yazılı ve metin tekil kullanıyor: contract.","fa":"«written» چاپ شده و متن مفرد آورده: contract."}},"remember":{"en":"Let the words around the gap tell you the kind of word, then copy one word exactly as the text has it.","tr":"Boşluğun etrafındaki kelimeler sana kelimenin türünü söylesin, sonra tek kelimeyi metindeki gibi aynen kopyala.","fa":"بگذار کلمه‌های دور جای خالی نوع کلمه را بگویند، بعد یک کلمه را دقیقاً مثل متن کپی کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x05-r2-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 2","title":{"en":"Meetings and a new shop","tr":"Toplantılar ve yeni bir dükkân","fa":"جلسه‌ها و یک مغازه‌ی تازه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT2-business"],"texts":[{"title":"Team meetings that work: advice for new supervisors","kind":"workplace advice","body":"Most people have sat through a meeting that wasted an hour of their working day. As a supervisor, you can make sure that your team's meetings are short, useful and even enjoyable. Here is what experienced managers recommend.\n\nBefore the meeting\nDecide whether you need a meeting at all: a quick message is often enough. If you do, send an agenda to everyone the day before, listing the topics in order and how long each one should take. Invite only the people who really need to be there; others can read the summary afterwards. Book a room that is the right size, and check that any equipment you need is working.\n\nKeep it short\nTry not to let any meeting run for longer than forty-five minutes. Research on the workplace suggests that people's concentration drops sharply after that point, and later decisions are often poorer as a result. If there is too much to cover, hold two shorter meetings rather than one long one.\n\nDuring the meeting\nStart on time, even if someone is late, and open by reminding everyone of the purpose of the meeting. When you discuss a problem, ask the quieter members of the team for their views first. This stops senior colleagues from dominating the discussion, and it often brings out ideas that would otherwise never be heard. Ask a different person to take the minutes each time, so that the job is shared fairly.\n\nFinishing well\nA meeting is only useful if something happens afterwards. In the last five minutes, go through each action that has been agreed and check who is responsible for it and by when. Then, within twenty-four hours, send everyone a short summary of the decisions, so that people who could not attend are kept informed.\n\nFinally, ask your team now and then what they think of your meetings. Their answers may surprise you."},{"title":"Opening a small shop: how to give it the best chance","kind":"business guide","body":"Many small shops close within their first two years, but most of the reasons are avoidable. This guide from the Halsey Business Centre sets out the steps that make the biggest difference.\n\nChoosing the location\nRent is usually your largest cost, so choose carefully. Before you sign a lease, spend a few days standing outside the shop at different times, counting how many people walk past. Retailers call this footfall, and a cheap shop on a quiet street is rarely a bargain. It is also worth finding out what the other shops nearby sell, so that you complement them rather than compete.\n\nManaging money\nEven successful shops are often slow to start. Make sure you have enough cash set aside to cover at least six months of expenses, including wages, energy and insurance, without relying on sales.\n\nBuying stock\nNew owners often fill every shelf on the first day. It is far better to start with a small range and order more of whatever sells. Too much stock ties up money that you may need for something else, and unsold goods soon look tired.\n\nBuilding loyal customers\nYour regular customers are your best advertisement. Invite them to leave their email addresses, and use these to send news of events and special offers, no more than twice a month. A handwritten thank-you note in a parcel costs almost nothing and is remembered for a long time.\n\nBeing found online\nEven if you sell nothing online, you need a simple website showing your opening hours, address and telephone number. Customers increasingly check before they set out, and a shop that cannot be found online may be assumed to have closed.\n\nGetting help\nYou do not have to do everything alone. The council's business advisers offer free one-to-one sessions for anyone who has opened a shop in the last three years, and they can often point you to grants you did not know about."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 15-21. Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"sentence","questions":[{"n":15,"kind":"gap","prompt":"An ___ should be sent to all those attending the day before the meeting.","accept":["agenda"],"limit":1,"evidence":"send an agenda to everyone the day before","why":{"en":"\"Send an agenda to everyone the day before.\" \"An\" before the gap needs a noun starting with a vowel.","tr":"\"Bir gün önce herkese bir gündem gönder.\" Boşluktan önceki \"An\" sesli harfle başlayan bir isim ister.","fa":"«روز قبل برای همه دستور جلسه بفرست». «An» قبل از جای خالی اسمی می‌خواهد که با حرف صدادار شروع شود."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"gap","prompt":"After forty-five minutes, people’s ___ falls considerably.","accept":["concentration"],"limit":1,"evidence":"people's concentration drops sharply after that point","why":{"en":"\"People’s concentration drops sharply\": falls considerably = drops sharply.","tr":"\"İnsanların dikkati keskin biçimde düşüyor\": falls considerably = drops sharply.","fa":"«تمرکز آدم‌ها به‌شدت پایین می‌آید»: falls considerably یعنی drops sharply."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"gap","prompt":"At the start, the supervisor should remind the team of the meeting’s ___.","accept":["purpose"],"limit":1,"evidence":"reminding everyone of the purpose of the meeting","why":{"en":"\"Open by reminding everyone of the purpose of the meeting.\"","tr":"\"Herkese toplantının amacını hatırlatarak başla.\"","fa":"«با یادآوری هدف جلسه به همه شروع کن»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Asking quieter staff first prevents ___ staff from dominating the discussion.","accept":["senior"],"limit":1,"evidence":"This stops senior colleagues from dominating the discussion","why":{"en":"\"This stops senior colleagues from dominating\": staff = colleagues, so the missing adjective is senior.","tr":"\"Bu, kıdemli çalışanların tartışmaya hâkim olmasını önler\": staff = colleagues; eksik sıfat senior.","fa":"«این جلوی میدان‌داری همکارهای ارشد را می‌گیرد»: staff یعنی colleagues، پس صفتِ جاافتاده senior است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The job of taking the ___ should be given to a different person each time.","accept":["minutes"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Ask a different person to take the minutes each time","why":{"en":"\"Take the minutes\": the written record of the meeting. Keep the s.","tr":"\"Tutanağı tutmak\": toplantının yazılı kaydı. s’yi koru.","fa":"«صورت‌جلسه نوشتن»: گزارش کتبی جلسه. s را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Before the end, check who is responsible for each ___.","accept":["action"],"limit":1,"evidence":"go through each action that has been agreed","why":{"en":"\"Go through each action that has been agreed and check who is responsible for it.\"","tr":"\"Kararlaştırılan her işi gözden geçir ve kimin sorumlu olduğunu kontrol et.\"","fa":"«هر کاری را که توافق شده مرور کن و ببین مسئولش کیست»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Staff who missed the meeting will be informed by a short ___.","accept":["summary"],"limit":1,"evidence":"send everyone a short summary of the decisions","why":{"en":"\"A short summary of the decisions... so that people who could not attend are kept informed.\" \"short\" is printed.","tr":"\"Kararların kısa bir özeti... katılamayanlar bilgilendirilsin diye.\" \"short\" yazılı.","fa":"«خلاصه‌ای کوتاه از تصمیم‌ها... تا کسانی که نتوانستند بیایند در جریان باشند». «short» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 22-27. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Starting a small shop","questions":[{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Location · before signing, count the people walking past, known as ___","accept":["footfall"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Retailers call this footfall","why":{"en":"\"Retailers call this footfall\": the number of people walking past.","tr":"\"Perakendeciler buna footfall der\": önünden geçen insan sayısı.","fa":"«خرده‌فروش‌ها به این footfall می‌گویند»: تعداد کسانی که از جلوی مغازه رد می‌شوند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":23,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Money · keep enough cash for six months of ___","accept":["expenses"],"limit":1,"evidence":"six months of expenses","why":{"en":"\"At least six months of expenses, including wages, energy and insurance\".","tr":"\"Maaşlar, enerji ve sigorta dahil en az altı aylık gider\".","fa":"«دست‌کم شش ماه هزینه، از جمله دستمزد، انرژی و بیمه»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Stock · avoid buying too much ___ at the start","accept":["stock"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Too much stock ties up money","why":{"en":"\"Too much stock ties up money\": the heading uses the same word, but the gap still needs it.","tr":"\"Fazla stok parayı bağlar\": başlık aynı kelimeyi kullanıyor ama boşluk yine onu istiyor.","fa":"«موجودیِ زیاد پول را قفل می‌کند»: عنوان همین کلمه را دارد، اما جای خالی باز هم آن را می‌خواهد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Customers · use email to tell them about events and special ___","accept":["offers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"send news of events and special offers","why":{"en":"\"News of events and special offers\". \"special\" is printed.","tr":"\"Etkinlik ve özel teklif haberleri\". \"special\" yazılı.","fa":"«خبر رویدادها و پیشنهادهای ویژه». «special» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Online · have a simple ___ with opening hours and address","accept":["website"],"limit":1,"evidence":"you need a simple website showing your opening hours","why":{"en":"\"A simple website showing your opening hours, address and telephone number\".","tr":"\"Açılış saatlerini, adresi ve telefonu gösteren basit bir web sitesi\".","fa":"«یک وب‌سایت ساده که ساعت کار، نشانی و تلفن را نشان دهد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":27,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Help · free sessions are offered by the council’s business ___","accept":["advisers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"The council's business advisers offer free one-to-one sessions","why":{"en":"\"The council’s business advisers offer free one-to-one sessions.\" Copy the spelling advisers.","tr":"\"Belediyenin iş danışmanları ücretsiz birebir görüşmeler sunuyor.\" advisers yazımını kopyala.","fa":"«مشاوران کسب‌وکار شهرداری جلسه‌های رایگان یک‌به‌یک می‌گذارند». املای advisers را کپی کن."},"trap":["TR-plural"]}]}],"id":"c-x05-r2-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Ask a different person to take the minutes.\" The minutes are...","options":["the written record of a meeting","the time limit of a meeting","the people invited"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Minutes = notes of what was said and decided.","tr":"Minutes = söylenen ve kararlaştırılanların notları.","fa":"minutes یعنی یادداشتِ آنچه گفته و تصمیم گرفته شد."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"Sentence: \"Concentration falls considerably after 45 minutes.\" Which words in a text mean the same?","options":["attention is best after 45 minutes","meetings should last 45 minutes","attention drops sharply after three quarters of an hour"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Falls considerably = drops sharply; 45 minutes = three quarters of an hour.","tr":"Falls considerably = keskin biçimde düşer; 45 dakika = üç çeyrek saat.","fa":"falls considerably یعنی drops sharply؛ ۴۵ دقیقه یعنی سه‌ربع ساعت."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Sentence: \"Send an ___ the day before.\" What kind of word fits?","options":["a verb","a noun beginning with a vowel sound","a plural noun"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"An\" comes before a singular noun that starts with a vowel sound.","tr":"\"An\", sesli bir sesle başlayan tekil bir isimden önce gelir.","fa":"«an» قبل از اسم مفردی می‌آید که با صدای مصوت شروع می‌شود."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Keep enough money for six months of rent and wages.\" Note: \"six months of ___\" (ONE WORD ONLY). Which answer breaks the limit?","options":["rent and wages","rent","wages"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"rent and wages\" is three words. With ONE WORD ONLY, the note must be written so that one word fits.","tr":"\"rent and wages\" üç kelime. ONE WORD ONLY varsa not, tek kelimenin uyacağı biçimde yazılmıştır.","fa":"«rent and wages» سه کلمه است. وقتی ONE WORD ONLY است، یادداشت طوری نوشته می‌شود که یک کلمه جا شود."}}],"id":"c-x05-r2-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r2"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
